{"entities":[{"text":"dobutamine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"dobutamine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"dobutamine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"Dubutamine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"Torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"congestive heart failure","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"heart failure","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"ventricular arrhythmias","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"QT prolongation","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"arrhythmias","label":"Disease","id":""}],"entity_aliases":[{"text":"dobutamine","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"Dubutamine","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"arrhythmias","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"QT prolongation","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"ventricular arrhythmias","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"Torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","id":"2","label":"Disease"},{"text":"heart failure","id":"3","label":"Disease"},{"text":"congestive heart failure","id":"3","label":"Disease"}],"filtered_entities":[{"text":"dobutamine","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"dilated cardiomyopathy","id":"2","label":"Disease"},{"text":"congestive heart failure","id":"3","label":"Disease"}],"gold_relations":"Dubutamine | CID | torsade de pointes","labels":"Chemical,Disease","metrics":{"precision":1.0,"recall":1.0,"f1":1.0,"tp":1,"fp":0,"fn":0,"rel_precision":1.0,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":1.0,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":0},"pairs":[{"head":"dobutamine","tail":"torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia","head_id":"1","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"dobutamine","tail":"dilated cardiomyopathy","head_id":"1","tail_id":"2"},{"head":"dobutamine","tail":"congestive heart failure","head_id":"1","tail_id":"3"}],"relations":["1 | 1"],"text":"Torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia during low dose intermittent dobutamine treatment in a patient with dilated cardiomyopathy and congestive heart failure. The authors describe the case of a 56-year-old woman with chronic, severe heart failure secondary to dilated cardiomyopathy and absence of significant ventricular arrhythmias who developed QT prolongation and torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia during one cycle of intermittent low dose (2.5 mcg/kg per min) dobutamine. This report of torsade de pointes ventricular tachycardia during intermittent dobutamine supports the hypothesis that unpredictable fatal arrhythmias may occur even with low doses and in patients with no history of significant rhythm disturbances. The mechanisms of proarrhythmic effects of Dubutamine are discussed."}